---
description: Rules for specs, tickets, roadmap and changelog
globs: docs/**/*.md,AGENTS.md
alwaysApply: false
---

You are editing project docs. Follow `AGENTS.md` (Docs rules, Feature workflow, Precedence).

- Specs (`docs/features/F<NN>-<slug>/spec.md`) hold requirements tagged Established (user-confirmed, implementable) or Proposed (awaiting confirmation), a Current behavior table marked Conforms / Conflicts / Unspecified, open questions, and a dated decisions log. Existing behavior is never a requirement by itself. Never fill a gap with an assumption: add an open question.
- Issues found outside the current task are reported to the user first. Write a ticket only after the user agrees; add to `docs/features/triage.md` only if the issue is still unresolved at the end of the conversation.
- Tickets (`docs/features/F<NN>-<slug>/tickets/M<n>-<NN>-<slug>.md`) are bounded tasks from `docs/features/_templates/ticket.md`. A ticket never adds a requirement the spec lacks.
- `docs/features/README.md` is the index. Keep statuses in sync with specs. New features get the next `F<NN>` ID there before their folder is created; IDs are never reused or renumbered.
- `docs/CHANGELOG.md` is shipped, verified history for external readers. Feature headings include the `F<NN>` ID and link the spec when one exists. No upcoming work, requirements, ticket or prototype links, or links to gitignored files.
- Legacy local docs (`CONTEXT.md`, `docs/adr/`, `docs/agents/`, `docs/specs/`) are historical input only. Verify them against code before reusing anything.
